.\n\n\"This collection of versions of Rumi by Andrew Harvey contains some of the master's most luminous verse, along with selections from his lesser-read prose works, with the aim of presenting a balanced view of his teaching that includes both the high-flying love of God and the rigorous path of discipline essential for those who seek it.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"latest_revision":12,"revision":12,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-03-31T16:40:00.151127"}}},"ISBN:9781851682515":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781851682515","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL21207331M/A_Rumi_anthology","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL21207331M/A_Rumi_anthology","details":{"publishers":["Oneworld"],"identifiers":{"librarything":["1714321"],"goodreads":["166803"]},"subtitle":"Rumi: poet and mystic tales of mystic meaning","series":["Oneworld spiritual classics"],"lc_classifications":["PK'6480'E5'N49'2000","PK6480.E5"],"key":"/books/OL21207331M","publish_places":["Oxford"],"contributions":["Nicholson, Reynold Alleyne, 1868-1945."],"subjects":["Jalal al-Din Rumi, Maulana, 1207-1273 -- Translations into English.","Sufism."],"pagination":"170 p.","source_records":["marc:marc_laurentian/openlibrary.mrc:380567393:942","bwb:9781851682515","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-007.mrc:88895306:1378","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2023-12-27:P9-BDR-778"],"title":"A Rumi anthology","notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"4"},"number_of_pages":170,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"isbn_10":["1851682511"],"publish_date":"2000","publish_country":"enk","by_statement":"translated by Reynold A. Nicholson.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL18999764W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"oclc_numbers":["44651964"],"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:P9-BDR-778"],"latest_revision":8,"revision":8,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-11-01T08:14:17.120947"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime